      <div class="label-stack">
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
  <h2>Caveats</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>If <b>sound</b> is missing from the prim&#39;s inventory and it is not a <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/UUID" target="_blank">UUID</a> or it is not a sound then an error is shouted on <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/DEBUG_CHANNEL" target="_blank">DEBUG_CHANNEL</a>.</li>
    <li>If <b>sound</b> is a <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/UUID" target="_blank">UUID</a> then there are no new <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Category:LSL_Permissions/Asset" target="_blank">asset permissions</a> consequences for the object.
    <ul>
      <li>The resulting object develops no new usage restrictions that might have occurred if the asset had been placed in the prims inventory.</li>
    </ul>
  
    </li>
    <li>This function is affected by the <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlSetSoundQueueing" target="_blank">Sound Queueing</a> property of the parent prim - this means it&#39;s possible to queue a slave sound prior to starting a master, without having to use more than one prim as an emitter. (See below).</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`-- for an uploaded .wav file called "MasterLoop" in inventory
ll.LoopSoundMaster("MasterLoop", 1.0)`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`// for an uploaded .wav file called "MasterLoop" in inventory
llLoopSoundMaster("MasterLoop", 1.0);`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <p>The script below is an example of how using <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlSetSoundQueueing" target="_blank">llSetSoundQueueing</a> affects the interaction between master and slave sounds. In the example, it is used to run a car engine.</p>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll = llcompat

local playState = 0  --see LUT below.

local lut = {"Engine start, idle.", "Accelerate, speed loop.", "Decelerate, idle.", "Idle, stop"}

local function main()
    ll.SetSoundQueueing(true)  --Set this so the we don't skip the 1st 'slave' sound.
end

function LLEvents.touch_start(events)
    local total_number = #events
    ll.Whisper(0, "Sound: " .. ll.List2String(lut, playState))
    if not (playState ~= 0) then  --start engine.
        ll.PlaySoundSlave("engine start", 1)  --This sound is skipped if Sound Queueing is not set.
        ll.LoopSoundMaster("idle", 1)
    elseif playState == 1 then  --accelerate, then play driving loop
        ll.PlaySoundSlave("accelerate", 1)
        ll.LoopSoundMaster("speed", 1)
    elseif playState == 2 then  --decelerate to idle.
        ll.PlaySoundSlave("decelerate", 1)
        ll.LoopSoundMaster("idle", 1)
    else  --stop the engine.
        ll.PlaySoundSlave("engine stop", 1)
        ll.Sleep(2)  --Wait until the above sound completes.
        ll.StopSound()  --Call this to prevent the master loop from restarting randomly (e.g. upon script reset or region change).
        playState = -1  --This actually resets to 0, as it's incremented below.
    end
    playState += 1  --increment playState.
end

main()
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`integer playState; //see LUT below.

list lut = ["Engine start, idle.","Accelerate, speed loop.","Decelerate, idle.", "Idle, stop"];

default
{
    state_entry()
    {
        llSetSoundQueueing(TRUE); //Set this so the we don't skip the 1st 'slave' sound.
    }

    touch_start(integer total_number)
    {
        llWhisper(0, "Sound: " + llList2String(lut,playState));
        if(!playState) //start engine.
        {
            llPlaySoundSlave("engine start",1); //This sound is skipped if Sound Queueing is not set.
            llLoopSoundMaster("idle",1);
        }
        else if(playState == 1) //accelerate, then play driving loop
        {
            llPlaySoundSlave("accelerate",1);
            llLoopSoundMaster("speed",1);
        }
        else if(playState == 2) //decelerate to idle.
        {
            llPlaySoundSlave("decelerate",1);
            llLoopSoundMaster("idle",1);
        }
        else //stop the engine.
        {
            llPlaySoundSlave("engine stop",1);
            llSleep(2); //Wait until the above sound completes.
            llStopSound(); //Call this to prevent the master loop from restarting randomly (e.g. upon script reset or region change).
            playState = -1; //This actually resets to 0, as it's incremented below.
        }
        ++playState; //increment playState.
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <p>The script below can be added to an object, to toggle a SoundMaster on and off. Note that the script requires a sound in inventory called MasterLoop, or you need to change the argument in the function for it to work.</p>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`--This integer (actually a boolean) will be used to manage the toggle effect.
local soundState = false
--Change MasterLoop to the sound clip you want to use.
local soundClip = "MasterLoop"
local function main()
    --Displays red "OFF" as floating text above the prim
    ll.SetText("OFF", vector(1, 0, 0), 1.0)
end
function LLEvents.touch_start(events)
    local num_detected = #events
    --When touched, soundState inverts its current boolean value. 1 becomes 0, 0 becomes 1. 
    soundState = not soundState
    if soundState then
        --Run this code when entering soundState 'on'
        --Displays green "ON" as floating text above the prim
        ll.SetText("ON", vector(0, 1, 0), 1.0)
        ll.LoopSoundMaster(soundClip, 1.0)
    else
        --Run this code when entering soundState 'off'
        --When touched, stop sound & display red "OFF" as floating text.
        ll.SetText("OFF", vector(1, 0, 0), 1.0)
        ll.StopSound()
    end
end

main()
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`//This integer (actually a boolean) will be used to manage the toggle effect.
integer soundState = FALSE;
//Change MasterLoop to the sound clip you want to use.
string soundClip = "MasterLoop";
default {
    state_entry()
    {
        //Displays red "OFF" as floating text above the prim
        llSetText("OFF", <1,0,0>, 1.0);
    }
    touch_start(integer num_detected)
    {
        //When touched, soundState inverts its current boolean value. 1 becomes 0, 0 becomes 1. 
        soundState = !soundState;
        if(soundState)
        {
            //Run this code when entering soundState 'on'
            //Displays green "ON" as floating text above the prim
            llSetText("ON", <0,1,0>, 1.0);
            llLoopSoundMaster(soundClip, 1.0);
        }else
        {   //Run this code when entering soundState 'off'
            //When touched, stop sound & display red "OFF" as floating text.
            llSetText("OFF", <1,0,0>, 1.0);
            llStopSound();
        }
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
